WEBVTT

00:16.410 --> 00:19.310
If my eyes are blinded by the sun

00:19.310 --> 00:23.990
I may just see the limits of the light.

00:23.990 --> 00:25.890
The mind of stardust

00:25.890 --> 00:31.730
What a small universe I live in

00:31.730 --> 00:39.270
Won't somebody give me
a code that starts at zero?

00:39.270 --> 00:41.840
Multiplied and in confusion

00:41.840 --> 00:45.870
A colony dead inside its cage

00:45.870 --> 00:50.350
Shoot your cowardly dreams

00:50.350 --> 00:53.520
Loneliness... self-destruct!

00:53.520 --> 00:57.920
No matter what sacrifices we make

00:57.920 --> 01:01.760
for a future just beyond reach

01:01.760 --> 01:05.430
Let our hearts speak to each other

01:05.430 --> 01:08.730
deep down inside

01:08.730 --> 01:12.870
Though the days just one step behind

01:12.870 --> 01:15.870
will pass even farther from us

01:15.870 --> 01:22.940
You will be in my thoughts

01:55.610 --> 01:58.450
Here.

01:58.450 --> 02:00.850
Thank you.

02:02.650 --> 02:05.590
Did you pick this flower yourself?

02:10.160 --> 02:13.160
Lia, wake up!

02:13.160 --> 02:14.190
Lia!

02:18.930 --> 02:20.270
Nadja...

02:20.270 --> 02:22.970
What a relief... you seem to be awake now.

02:22.970 --> 02:24.770
Are you all right?

02:24.770 --> 02:26.370
Ow!

02:28.210 --> 02:31.050
So you saved me, Nadja?

02:31.050 --> 02:34.950
I may be a halfbreed,
but I'm still a beastman...

02:34.950 --> 02:39.850
and saving you from falling to
the valley floor was a piece of cake.

02:39.850 --> 02:42.850
Thank you. I'm grateful for that.

02:45.790 --> 02:49.630
However... I wonder
what the deal with this cave is.

02:49.630 --> 02:51.870
I'm glad we're out of
danger for the time being...

02:51.870 --> 02:56.470
but for a while now I've been
having strange visions come and go.

02:56.470 --> 02:59.980
Visions of people I'd
forgotten about a long time ago.

02:59.980 --> 03:02.880
This is the Labyrinth of Memories.

03:02.880 --> 03:06.480
I just saw a vision of my own past...

03:06.480 --> 03:08.510
something I'd forgotten all about.

03:09.850 --> 03:14.750
There are Two Kinds of Futures"

03:18.560 --> 03:22.200
I'll be taking the Destruct
Code now, and no funny stuff!

03:22.200 --> 03:23.370
It's not here!

03:23.370 --> 03:24.930
She's telling the truth, bear-o!

03:24.930 --> 03:27.740
The Destruct Code was
taken by the Alligator Master!

03:27.740 --> 03:29.740
What's that?!

03:29.740 --> 03:34.070
It looks like the Alligator Master
betrayed the Salvation Committee, no?

03:38.850 --> 03:42.350
Don't believe their ramblings!

03:42.350 --> 03:44.850
Alligator Master... it was you!

03:44.850 --> 03:48.720
If this is what you want,
then take it... it's yours.

03:51.530 --> 03:56.690
But in exchange, I claim custody of
the three from the Destruction Committee.

03:58.700 --> 04:03.610
So what you're saying is that
you met Kyrie over 300 years ago?

04:03.610 --> 04:07.310
That's right. It was before
I'd even reached 100 years old.

04:07.310 --> 04:11.880
I'd gone picking flowers in
Dragon Valley and was on my way home.

04:11.880 --> 04:13.820
I was crying because I'd fallen down...

04:13.820 --> 04:16.480
and Kyrie came up and
said some nice things to me.

04:16.480 --> 04:20.560
What's more, he looked
exactly like he still looks now.

04:20.560 --> 04:23.460
Except... his hair was different.

04:23.460 --> 04:26.660
It was so red it was like it was on fire.

04:26.660 --> 04:31.630
So what does that mean?
That Kyrie hasn't aged at all?

04:31.630 --> 04:34.470
There's no way he's a
Dragon like you, is there?

04:34.470 --> 04:39.140
No. If he were a Dragon,
I would've known it when I saw him.

04:39.140 --> 04:41.410
So if he's not a Dragon...

04:41.410 --> 04:48.180
Some other creature that lives just as
long as a Dragon? There shouldn't be one.

04:48.180 --> 04:49.840
Perhaps...

04:51.990 --> 04:56.250
I think we may have been gravely mistaken.

05:15.640 --> 05:17.270
Ow... ow...

05:18.510 --> 05:22.350
Cease this futile display of
resistance and come with me quietly!

05:22.350 --> 05:27.020
Or would you rather not
know the secret of the Destruct Code?

05:27.020 --> 05:30.160
The secret of the Destruct Code?

05:30.160 --> 05:34.300
Exactly! You don't seem
to know what it is yet...

05:34.300 --> 05:39.470
but I have unlocked the
secret of the Destruct Code!

05:39.470 --> 05:42.800
Now then, you're coming with me!

05:47.840 --> 05:49.240
Toppy!

05:49.240 --> 05:50.640
Bear-o!

05:56.420 --> 05:59.410
Morte! We're pulling out for now, bear-o!

06:00.220 --> 06:04.250
We can't go yet! I have to
get the Destruct Code back first!

06:10.060 --> 06:11.200
What?!

06:11.200 --> 06:13.570
Don't let 'em get away! After them!

06:18.610 --> 06:20.410
What did the Alligator Master mean just now...

06:20.410 --> 06:23.280
when he was talking about the
"secret" of the Destruct Code, bear-o?!

06:23.280 --> 06:24.710
I don't know.

06:24.710 --> 06:28.120
But my guess is... what Morte has right now...

06:28.120 --> 06:30.420
may not be the actual Destruct Code!

06:30.420 --> 06:33.050
What're you talking about?!
After all we've gone through!

06:33.050 --> 06:36.560
But why else would the
Alligator Master come back...

06:36.560 --> 06:41.030
and deliberately bring back
what he'd already taken from us?!

06:41.030 --> 06:43.600
This is definitely the Destruct Code!

06:43.600 --> 06:45.930
It's the real thing... I know it is!

06:47.100 --> 06:49.470
Now that we're in the
Labyrinth of Memories again...

06:49.470 --> 06:51.870
if I can just see that memory one more time...

06:51.870 --> 06:54.040
I might be able to figure it out!

06:54.040 --> 06:56.240
What do you mean by "that memory," bear-o?!

06:56.240 --> 06:59.710
The memory of Morte's
brother getting the Destruct Code!

06:59.710 --> 07:04.090
What... you're saying you
were there when Reve died?!

07:04.090 --> 07:08.090
Apparently. But I didn't remember it.

07:08.090 --> 07:10.630
I still can't remember it, even now.

07:10.630 --> 07:14.960
I'm not even sure if I was really there.

07:19.400 --> 07:20.630
Gimme that!

07:46.430 --> 07:48.000
It's a beastman attack!

07:48.000 --> 07:49.690
Grab your weapons!

08:11.390 --> 08:13.350
Kyrie!

08:13.350 --> 08:14.980
Reve?

08:22.360 --> 08:27.500
What're you still doing here?!
You were supposed to have left for Tomai!

08:27.500 --> 08:30.510
It would've been a pointless trip anyway.

08:30.510 --> 08:33.370
I just thought I'd stay here
a little while longer instead.

08:33.370 --> 08:35.910
Why?! What do you mean?

08:35.910 --> 08:42.520
I wanted to see whether you guys'd
really be able to change the world or not.

08:42.520 --> 08:44.090
Whatever... but it's dangerous here!

08:44.090 --> 08:48.390
The beastmen found us, so you
need to go hide somewhere, Kyrie!

08:51.890 --> 08:54.730
Who are you?

08:56.330 --> 08:59.070
You still can't remember?

08:59.070 --> 09:02.940
All right... in that case I'll just tell you.

09:02.940 --> 09:05.870
That black ball that Morte's
been carrying around all this time...

09:05.870 --> 09:09.110
isn't the Destruct Code.

09:09.110 --> 09:11.740
The real Destruct Code is...

09:22.260 --> 09:24.620
Morte! Wake up, bear-o!

09:28.300 --> 09:29.890
Where are we?

09:32.700 --> 09:34.870
I see you're awake now.

09:34.870 --> 09:36.870
Where's Kyrie, bear-o?!

09:36.870 --> 09:41.440
How should I know?
Probably still buried somewhere in that cave...

09:41.440 --> 09:45.380
reveling in bygone memories of happier days.

09:45.380 --> 09:48.920
More importantly, I need the
two of you to tell me something.

09:48.920 --> 09:52.450
What did he mean by the
"secret of the Destruct Code"?

09:52.450 --> 09:54.660
What does that Alligator Master know?

09:54.660 --> 09:58.260
How do you use this?!

09:58.260 --> 10:01.420
I keep telling you... I don't know.

10:02.800 --> 10:05.490
In that case, I'll just
have to make you remember!

10:07.270 --> 10:09.500
N-No! D-Don't, bear-o!

11:28.850 --> 11:31.720
Why are you stopping all of a sudden?

11:36.890 --> 11:38.480
Kyrie...

11:40.660 --> 11:45.200
There's something I'd like to ask you.

11:45.200 --> 11:47.270
Is it possible that you're the...?

11:47.270 --> 11:52.000
That's right. He's the Destruct Code!

11:59.280 --> 12:01.280
What happened to Morte and Toppy?

12:01.280 --> 12:03.720
They're with the Eagle Master.

12:03.720 --> 12:05.520
And right now those
Salvation Committee nincompoops...

12:05.520 --> 12:09.890
are trying to get that girl to tell
them the secret of the Destruct Code.

12:09.890 --> 12:14.060
Even though of course the real
Destruct Code is standing right here.

12:16.400 --> 12:22.060
Now then, come along with me...
we're going to create a new world.

12:23.300 --> 12:27.110
Before we get to the question of
what to do with the Destruct Code...

12:27.110 --> 12:30.610
there's the little matter
of payback from before.

12:30.610 --> 12:33.410
You two! You're trying to stand in my way?!

12:33.410 --> 12:37.420
If I recall correctly, it was
you who betrayed us first.

12:37.420 --> 12:39.980
You stupid little fool!

12:46.260 --> 12:48.130
Good grief.

12:48.130 --> 12:49.820
At any rate, Kyrie...

13:04.010 --> 13:05.240
Bear-o?

13:06.310 --> 13:08.950
What say you try remembering now, eh?

13:08.950 --> 13:13.420
It's like I keep saying... I don't know.

13:13.420 --> 13:16.960
Well, that suits me just fine.
The longer it takes you to remember...

13:16.960 --> 13:20.090
the more fun I get to
have wringing it out of you!

13:23.760 --> 13:24.920
What's going on?

13:26.630 --> 13:28.260
What the hell's going on?!

13:41.220 --> 13:43.880
H-How dare you!

13:51.030 --> 13:52.860
Kyrie!

13:52.860 --> 13:55.030
Are you all right? Both of you?

13:55.030 --> 13:59.170
Kyrie, your hair... what, are you
some kind of punk now, bear-o?!

13:59.170 --> 14:03.900
We'll talk later. Right now you need
to get as far away from here as possible.

14:03.900 --> 14:05.810
What?! Wait a minute!

14:05.810 --> 14:06.870
The Destruct Code!

14:06.870 --> 14:09.040
Morte...

14:09.040 --> 14:13.750
Don't worry about that anymore.
It's not what you think it is, Morte.

14:13.750 --> 14:17.490
What do you mean, bear-o?!

14:17.490 --> 14:20.660
This ball isn't the Destruct Code.

14:20.660 --> 14:23.760
It's the storage medium for the Destruct Code.

14:23.760 --> 14:27.530
The true Destruct Code is me.

14:27.530 --> 14:28.860
Huh?!

14:28.860 --> 14:30.930
What're you talking about, bear-o?!

14:30.930 --> 14:33.000
What does that mean?!

14:33.000 --> 14:36.000
In the course of my travels,
I visited the Golden Lions' camp.

14:36.000 --> 14:39.440
That's where I met your brother.

14:39.440 --> 14:45.710
When he said he'd found the
Destruct Code, he wasn't referring to that ball.

14:45.710 --> 14:49.080
He was talking about meeting me.

14:49.080 --> 14:55.190
I got caught up in the explosions there
and wound up losing my storage medium.

14:55.190 --> 14:59.960
That's how it ended up with Reve's coffin...
and eventually in your hands.

15:02.300 --> 15:10.300
Having totally forgotten who I was,
I headed for Tomai as plain Kyrie Illnis.

15:10.300 --> 15:14.910
And that's where I met you, Morte.

15:14.910 --> 15:16.540
That's crazy...!

15:18.610 --> 15:20.920
What's this?!

15:20.920 --> 15:25.220
These are my true memories.

15:25.220 --> 15:27.490
I've been alive ever since the world was born...

15:27.490 --> 15:31.050
for tens of thousands of years,
and these are my memories.

15:34.060 --> 15:38.170
So you're the Destruct Code...

15:38.170 --> 15:42.300
which means you have
the power to destroy the world?

15:42.300 --> 15:48.410
As the Destruct Code, I've existed on
this world for tens of thousands of years.

15:48.410 --> 15:52.280
I have the power to reset the world.

15:52.280 --> 15:55.450
Whenever someone
believes in the Destruct Code...

15:55.450 --> 15:58.920
and truly wants the world destroyed...

15:58.920 --> 16:01.480
that's when my power activates.

16:05.490 --> 16:10.160
That man is the Destruct Code! Secure him!

16:15.100 --> 16:16.360
Kyrie!

16:28.520 --> 16:31.610
You goddamn spook!

16:35.060 --> 16:37.110
W-Wait! I'm the...

16:40.630 --> 16:42.200
Is this...?

16:42.200 --> 16:47.630
The true Kyrie's Destruct Code power, bear-o?!

16:48.070 --> 16:53.870
When someone hopes for it strongly
enough, the Destruct Code activates.

16:53.870 --> 16:57.910
Morte believed in the existence
of the Destruct Code all this time...

16:57.910 --> 17:00.900
and wished for world destruction.

17:07.190 --> 17:12.990
Ever since that moment,
the Destruct Code has been active.

17:15.730 --> 17:17.060
You have to wait, bear-o!

17:17.060 --> 17:18.330
Kyrie!

17:26.540 --> 17:32.000
So this is it... this is the
power of the Destruct Code!

17:33.050 --> 17:35.070
Watch out! Nadja!

17:37.080 --> 17:39.710
Kyrie! Stop this, bear-o!

17:40.690 --> 17:42.590
Kyrie!

17:42.590 --> 17:43.960
Hey!

17:45.860 --> 17:47.360
Agan!

17:47.360 --> 17:50.600
I come here on a simple
food delivery for the Walruses!

17:50.600 --> 17:52.770
What the hell's going on?!

17:52.770 --> 17:54.640
Whoa, you two!

17:54.640 --> 17:57.070
Hey! You wanna ride with me, you gotta pay up!

17:57.070 --> 18:01.030
This is no time to be haggling!
Now hurry up and let us on, bear-o!

18:07.750 --> 18:12.250
If this keeps up, the whole world'll
be reset as nothing but a sea of sand!

18:12.250 --> 18:15.590
Well, isn't this what you wished for?

18:15.590 --> 18:17.490
Is this...

18:17.490 --> 18:20.550
Is this the world I wished for?

18:31.810 --> 18:34.110
Kyrie...

18:34.110 --> 18:38.010
Morte!

18:49.090 --> 18:52.290
I activated the Destruct Code.

18:52.290 --> 18:54.660
I activated Kyrie.

18:58.600 --> 19:01.830
Am I all right with the
world ending right now?

19:02.700 --> 19:06.260
Am I really all right with that?

19:13.010 --> 19:16.380
The world keeps right on changing.

19:16.380 --> 19:22.520
After this, you guys are going
to change the world even more.

19:22.520 --> 19:27.700
Go on to build the kind of future
where everyone can live in happiness.

19:27.700 --> 19:32.460
You're not alone anymore,
so I think you're gonna be okay.

19:47.720 --> 19:51.320
That's enough.

19:51.320 --> 19:54.050
The world doesn't have to end.

19:57.090 --> 19:59.750
It's fine the way it is.

20:01.900 --> 20:05.390
I'll live in the world as it is from now on.

20:08.340 --> 20:09.890
So...

20:11.110 --> 20:12.730
please.

20:38.600 --> 20:40.230
Kyrie?

20:41.700 --> 20:43.530
Morte.

20:57.280 --> 21:00.150
When the gods created the world...

21:00.150 --> 21:04.730
they also created a
Destruct Code to bring it to ruin.

21:04.730 --> 21:06.630
So that if someone who believed
in the Destruct Code's existence...

21:06.630 --> 21:10.430
and truly wished for the
world's destruction should appear...

21:10.430 --> 21:15.340
the Destruct Code would be activated,
and the world would be reset.

21:15.340 --> 21:20.770
The gods placed the decision in the
hands of the humans and beastmen.

21:22.610 --> 21:26.110
And the world was saved.

21:26.110 --> 21:29.580
But that doesn't mean
that the world was changed.

21:29.580 --> 21:34.490
A small privileged class of beastmen
still monopolize and control all the wealth.

21:34.490 --> 21:36.920
And humans are still oppressed.

21:36.920 --> 21:40.490
The Destruct Code has no
power to change the world.

21:40.490 --> 21:44.090
We are the ones who change the world.

21:45.500 --> 21:48.170
There are two kinds of futures.

21:48.170 --> 21:51.610
A bright, shining future...
and a future of utter darkness.

21:51.610 --> 21:57.010
But even if the future of utter
darkness awaits us, there's nothing to fear.

21:57.010 --> 22:00.510
Because hope exists in both futures.

22:00.510 --> 22:07.320
And because the future
continually changes through hope.

22:09.860 --> 22:11.460
Huh? Bear-o?

22:11.460 --> 22:15.190
Hey, what are you trying to act all cool for?

22:21.030 --> 22:24.540
The glimmering seas of sand

22:24.540 --> 22:27.670
The end of the green earth

22:27.670 --> 22:33.750
Memories overflowing from the sky

22:33.750 --> 22:36.920
now plunged into darkness

22:36.920 --> 22:40.150
The memories will pile up

22:40.150 --> 22:46.160
like mounds of rubble

22:46.160 --> 22:49.330
Mutual encounters

22:49.330 --> 22:52.400
Misunderstood feelings

22:52.400 --> 22:55.540
Interwoven words

22:55.540 --> 22:58.670
People hurting each other

22:58.670 --> 23:10.780
Does the path we walk on
still lead us to tomorrow?

23:13.620 --> 23:17.460
Living this moment against the world

23:17.460 --> 23:20.530
isn't just about changing the world

23:20.530 --> 23:26.070
We're off on a distant journey across the waves

23:26.070 --> 23:29.640
So let our living heartbeat echo in the wind

23:29.640 --> 23:33.140
Around the world, to the end of the world

23:33.140 --> 23:39.110
Until we reach

23:39.110 --> 23:50.720
the promised land just beyond
